{"version":"2026.10.11-r25","id":"Q82906133","formula":"NaOD","hill":"HNaO","elements":["H","O","Na"],"composition":{"H":1.0,"O":1.0,"Na":1.0},"names":{"en":"Sodium deuteroxide","ru":"Дейтероксид натрия"},"descriptions":{"en":"Sodium deuteroxide or deuterated sodium hydroxide is a chemical compound with the formula NaOD or NaO2H. IUPAC recommends that the symbol for deuterium should be 2H, although most chemists use the term NaOD. It is a white solid very similar to sodium hydroxide, of which it is an isotopologue. It is used as a strong base and deuterium source in the production of other deuterated compounds. For example, reaction with chloral hydrate gives deuterated chloroform, and reaction with N-nitrosodimethylamine gives the deuterated analog of that compound.","ru":"Дейтерокси́д на́трия — неорганическое химическое соединение натрия и оксида дейтерия с формулой NaO 2 H {\\displaystyle {\\ce {NaO^2H}}} или NaOD {\\displaystyle {\\ce {NaOD}}} , являющееся изотопной разновидностью гидроксида натрия, в которой атом водорода замещён дейтерием. Представляет собой белое гигроскопичное кристаллическое вещество, обладающее сильными основными свойствами."},"fame":5,"pubchemCid":23676750,"mass":41.003,"charge":0,"smiles":"[2H][O-].[Na+]","inchikey":"HEMHJVSKTPXQMS-DYCDLGHISA-M","iupac":null,"classes":[{"qid":"Q113145171","names":{"en":"type of chemical entity","ru":"тип химического объекта","uk":"тип хімічної сутності"}}],"structureInfo":{"kind":"crystal","source":"materialsproject","ref":"mp-23891","atoms":18,"license":"CC BY 4.0, Materials Project"},"structure":{"cell":[[3.369,0.0,0.0],[0.0,10.903,0.0],[0.0,0.0,3.353]],"kind":"crystal","atoms":[{"x":1.684,"y":1.752,"z":0.838,"el":"Na"},{"x":0.0,"y":3.699,"z":2.515,"el":"Na"},{"x":3.369,"y":3.699,"z":2.515,"el":"Na"},{"x":1.684,"y":4.994,"z":0.838,"el":"H"},{"x":0.0,"y":0.457,"z":2.515,"el":"H"},{"x":3.369,"y":0.457,"z":2.515,"el":"H"},{"x":0.0,"y":1.422,"z":2.515,"el":"O"},{"x":3.369,"y":1.422,"z":2.515,"el":"O"},{"x"